+/*
+ * The Daily Grind – lightweight client-side analytics.
+ *
+ * Records page views and click interactions, then coalesces them into a
+ * single batched background request:
+ *   - Events are queued in memory.
+ *   - Each new event resets a debounce timer (DEBOUNCE_MS), so bursts of
+ *     rapid interactions collapse into one request.
+ *   - MAX_WAIT_MS caps how long events can sit in the queue during a
+ *     continuous stream of activity; MAX_BATCH forces an early flush.
+ *   - The send itself is deferred to browser idle time and uses
+ *     navigator.sendBeacon (falling back to fetch keepalive), so it never
+ *     blocks interaction or navigation.
+ *   - Pending events are flushed when the page is hidden/unloaded.
+ *
+ * Privacy: honours Do Not Track / Global Privacy Control, never records
+ * form values, and strips query strings / fragments from URLs.
+ */
