+# Old-origin files (https://app.dailygrind.coffee)
+
+Deploy these to the **old** origin. They pair with `/manifest.webmanifest`
+(`migrate_from`) and `/settings-migration.js` on the new origin
+(https://www.dailygrind.coffee). Both origins share the `dailygrind.coffee`
+registrable domain. Origin migration needs that same-site relationship.
+
+| File | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `.well-known/web-app-origin-association` | Lets the new app's manifest ID take over this installation. Serve as `application/json` over HTTPS. |
+| `manifest.webmanifest` | Replaces the old manifest. `migrate_to` tells the browser about the move before users visit the new site. |
+| `settings-bridge.html` | Gives localStorage settings only to the new origin, so user configuration carries over. Must not send `X-Frame-Options: DENY` or a `frame-ancestors` that excludes `https://www.dailygrind.coffee`. |
+| `migration-banner.js` | Fallback banner for browsers without origin migration (Firefox, Safari). Include it on every old-origin page. |
+
+Keep the old origin serving these files (don't redirect them) until the
+installed base has migrated.
+
+To make the move mandatory, add `"behavior": "force"` to the `migrate_from` entry
+in the new manifest. Users will then have to choose Update or Remove.
