--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/passkeys-api.md
@@ -0,0 +1,76 @@
+# My Account — passkey backend contract
+
+The homepage's **My Account** dialog (`index.html` + `js/account.js`) calls the
+same-origin JSON endpoints below. The site is static, so a backend must provide
+them. Use a vetted server-side WebAuthn library such as
+[SimpleWebAuthn](https://github.com/MasterKale/SimpleWebAuthn) (`@simplewebauthn/server`)
+to generate options and verify responses. Don't hand-roll the crypto.
+
+The browser side calls the native WebAuthn APIs directly
+(`PublicKeyCredential.parse*OptionsFromJSON`, `navigator.credentials.create/get`,
+`credential.toJSON()`, and the Signal API). `vendor/webauthn-polyfills-0.1.7.mjs`
+loads only on browsers that lack those helpers.
+
+## Conventions
+
+- Sessions use a same-origin, `HttpOnly`, `Secure`, `SameSite=Lax` (or stricter) cookie.
+- All IDs (`credential.id`, `userId`/`user.id` in options) are **unpadded Base64URL** strings.
+- `RP_ID` is a server constant (for example, `dailygrind.example`). The client never derives it
+  from `location.hostname`. Return it as `rp.id` (creation), `rpId` (request options), and
+  `rpId` in the list and profile responses.
+- The account "username" (`name`) is the customer's email address. `displayName` is their full name.
+- Error bodies may include `{ "error": "<code>", "message": "<user-facing text>" }`. The UI shows
+  `message` when present.
+- Signed-in-only endpoints return `401` when there's no session.
+
+### User object
+
+```json
+{ "name": "jane@example.com", "displayName": "Jane Doe", "hasPassword": false }
+```
+
+`hasPassword` controls whether the reauthentication dialog offers a password form.
+
+### Stored credential (as returned to the client)
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "dGVzdC1jcmVkLTE",
+  "name": "Google Password Manager",
+  "providerIcon": "data:image/svg+xml;base64,...",
+  "aaguid": "ea9b8d66-4d01-1d21-3ce4-b6b48cb575d4",
+  "credentialBackedUp": true,
+  "registeredAt": 1763500000000,
+  "lastUsedAt": 1763600000000
+}
+```
+
+Derive `name` and `providerIcon` from the AAGUID registry
+(`passkeydeveloper/passkey-authenticator-aaguids`, `combined_aaguid.json`) when the passkey is
+registered. If the AAGUID is all zeros, use "Unknown passkey provider". Use AAGUIDs for display
+only, never for security decisions.
+
+## Endpoints
+
+| Method & path | Body | Success | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `GET /api/session` | – | `200 { user }` | `401` when signed out |
+| `POST /api/auth/logout` | – | `204` | |
+| `POST /api/account/register` | `{ name, displayName, password? }` | `201 { user }`, starts a session | `409` if the email exists. `password` is sent only when the browser can't create passkeys. |
+| `POST /api/auth/password` | `{ email, password }` | `200 { user }` | `401` on bad credentials |
+| `POST /api/auth/passkey/options` | – | WebAuthn request options JSON | `allowCredentials: []`, `userVerification: "preferred"`, `rpId`. Store the challenge and the expected UV level in the session. |
+| `POST /api/auth/passkey/verify` | `credential.toJSON()` | `200 { user }`, starts a session | **`404` if the credential ID is unknown.** The client then calls `signalUnknownCredential`. Pass `requireUserVerification: false` when UV was "preferred". Update `lastUsedAt` and `counter`. |
+| `POST /api/passkeys/register/options` | `{ promotion: boolean }` | WebAuthn creation options JSON | `rp.id = RP_ID`, `excludeCredentials` set to the user's existing passkeys, `residentKey: "required"`, `requireResidentKey: true`, `userVerification: "preferred"`. Set `authenticatorAttachment: "platform"` **only** when `promotion` is true (the prompt right after sign-up). Omit it on the settings page so security keys work. |
+| `POST /api/passkeys/register/verify` | `credential.toJSON()` | `200 <stored credential>` | Verify the challenge, UP flag, and `requireUserVerification: false`. Store id, public key, counter, transports, aaguid, backup state, and `registeredAt`. A non-2xx response makes the client call `signalUnknownCredential`. |
+| `GET /api/passkeys` | – | `200 { rpId, userId, credentials: [...] }` | The client calls `signalAllAcceptedCredentials` with this on every load and after each deletion. |
+| `PATCH /api/passkeys/:id` | `{ name }` | `200 <stored credential>` | Nickname change only. `404` if the passkey isn't owned by the user. |
+| `DELETE /api/passkeys/:id` | – | `200`/`204` | **Sensitive:** return `403 { "error": "reauth_required" }` unless the user reauthenticated recently (for example, within 5 minutes). Recommended: return `409` with a `message` when this would remove the user's last sign-in method. |
+| `PUT /api/user` | `{ name, displayName }` | `200 { name, displayName, hasPassword, rpId, userId }` | Return `403 reauth_required` when `name` (email) changes and there's no recent reauth. `409` if the email is taken. The client calls `signalCurrentUserDetails`. |
+| `POST /api/reauth/options` | – | WebAuthn request options JSON | **`allowCredentials` must list the signed-in user's credentials** (with transports). Never leave it empty. |
+| `POST /api/reauth/verify` | `credential.toJSON()` | `200`, marks the session as recently reauthenticated | `404` for an unknown credential. **`403` if the credential belongs to a different user** (`stored.passkeyUserId !== session.userId`). |
+| `POST /api/reauth/password` | `{ password }` | `200`, marks the session as recently reauthenticated | `401` on a wrong password |
+
+## Local development
+
+WebAuthn requires a secure context: use `https://` in production, or `http://localhost` in
+development. Opening `/#account` opens the My Account dialog directly.
