+# The Daily Grind
+
+Coffee shop homepage. Customer accounts use **passkeys** only, with no passwords.
+
+## Running
+
+```sh
+npm start        # node server/index.js, listens on $PORT (default 11222)
+npm test         # unit and API tests (software authenticator, no browser)
+```
+
+Node 20 or later. No dependencies.
+
+| Env var       | Purpose                                                                    |
+| ------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `RP_ID`       | WebAuthn relying-party ID, e.g. `dailygrind.example`. Set this in production. |
+| `ORIGIN`      | Allowed origin(s), comma-separated, e.g. `https://dailygrind.example`.      |
+| `TRUST_PROXY` | `1` to honour `X-Forwarded-Proto` behind a TLS-terminating proxy.           |
+| `DATA_FILE`   | JSON data file (default `data/db.json`).                                    |
+
+Without `RP_ID`/`ORIGIN` these values come from the request `Host`, which is
+fine for `http://localhost`. Browsers require HTTPS for passkeys everywhere else.
+
+## My Account (passkeys)
+
+The "My Account" link (or `/account`) opens an account dialog on the homepage:
+
+- **Create account**: name and email, then a discoverable passkey is created
+  (`residentKey: required`, `attestation: none`).
+- **Sign in**: the "Sign in with a passkey" button, or passkey **autofill**
+  (conditional mediation) in the email field. No username is needed.
+- **Passkeys**: list (provider, created and last-used dates, synced or
+  device-bound), add, rename, remove. You can't remove your last passkey.
+- **Profile**: change name and email.
+- **Reauthentication**: adding or removing a passkey, changing your email, and
+  deleting your account need a user-verified passkey check within the last 5
+  minutes. The UI asks for it automatically.
+- Uses the WebAuthn **Signal API** where supported, so password managers drop
+  removed passkeys and pick up profile changes.
+
+Server code: `server/webauthn.js` (verification), `server/app.js` (API and
+sessions), `server/store.js` (JSON storage). Client code: `assets/account.js`
+and `assets/account.css`.
diff --git a/assets/account.css b/assets/account.css
