 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Passkeys
+
+Sign-in, sign-up and account settings (`/account`) support passkeys (WebAuthn):
+
+- **Sign in** – passkey suggestions in the username field's autofill (conditional UI), plus a "Sign in with a passkey" button. After a password sign-in, supporting password managers can silently create a passkey (conditional create).
+- **Sign up** – after creating an account, users are offered to create a passkey.
+- **Account settings** – list, rename and delete passkeys, create new ones (security keys included), and update the display name. Changes are synced to password managers via the WebAuthn Signal API.
+- **Reauthentication** – creating or deleting a passkey more than 5 minutes after signing in requires confirming with an existing passkey (or the password as a fallback).
+
+Password sign-in/sign-up is proxied through `/api/auth/*` so the server can keep a session; WebAuthn verification uses [SimpleWebAuthn](https://simplewebauthn.dev/). Passkey records are stored in `.data/passkeys.json` (override with `PASSKEY_DATA_DIR`).
+
+| Variable | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `PASSKEY_RP_ID` | Relying Party ID, e.g. `astro-news-pytrpecapa-uc.a.run.app`. Defaults to the request host. |
+| `PASSKEY_ORIGINS` | Comma-separated list of allowed origins. Defaults to the request origin. |
+| `PASSKEY_DATA_DIR` | Directory for the passkey store. Defaults to `./.data`. |
+
+Passkeys need a secure context: `https://` in production or `http://localhost` in development.
