 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Passkeys
+
+Sign-in, sign-up, and account settings support [passkeys](https://passkeys.dev/) (WebAuthn), built with
+[SimpleWebAuthn](https://simplewebauthn.dev/):
+
+- **Sign up** (`/signup`) with a passkey only, or with a password (followed by a prompt to add a passkey).
+- **Sign in** (`/signin`) with the "Sign in with a passkey" button or via passkey autofill in the username
+  field (conditional mediation). After a password sign-in the app tries an automatic passkey upgrade
+  (conditional create) and otherwise offers to create one.
+- **Manage** passkeys in account settings (`/account`): create, rename, and remove them. Each passkey shows its
+  provider (from the FIDO Convenience Metadata Service by AAGUID), whether it's synced, and when it was created
+  and last used.
+- **Reauthentication**: creating or removing a passkey requires a sign-in within the last 5 minutes; otherwise
+  the user confirms it's them with a passkey or their password.
+- The [Signal API](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/webauthn-signal-api) keeps password managers in
+  sync when passkeys are removed or unknown.
+
+Passwords are still verified by the upstream Times auth API, but that now happens on the server, which
+then creates the session. Local user records and passkeys are stored in `.data/auth-store.json`.
+
+| Environment variable | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `PASSKEY_RP_ID` | Relying party ID (defaults to the request hostname) |
+| `PASSKEY_ORIGINS` | Comma-separated allowed origins (defaults to the request origin, plus its `https://` form) |
+| `AUTH_DATA_DIR` | Directory for the auth store (defaults to `./.data`) |
+| `PASSKEY_PROVIDER_METADATA` | Set to `off` to skip downloading passkey provider names and icons |
