+# Privacy by Design — The Daily Grind website
+
+This file documents how the public site handles personal data and why. Re-run
+`pnpm run audit:privacy` before every release. It fails the build if a third-party
+request, tracker, inline script/style, GET logout, or CSP drift gets in.
+
+## Principles
+
+1. **Collect nothing by default.** The marketing pages set no cookies, use no
+   analytics, and load no third-party code. The browser never sends data anywhere
+   except our own origin.
+2. **First-party only.** Images, CSS and JS are self-hosted under `/assets/`.
+   Fonts are system fonts. The Content-Security-Policy enforces this, so any
+   third-party resource that sneaks in gets blocked.
+3. **Honor user signals.** Global Privacy Control (and legacy DNT) is detected,
+   acknowledged in the footer, and published in `/.well-known/gpc.json`.
+4. **Minimize what lingers.** Personal-data pages are `no-store`. Logout is a
+   POST that triggers `Clear-Site-Data`, and the client also wipes `dg:*` Web
+   Storage keys. PII and click-ID query parameters are removed from the URL bar.
+5. **Least privilege for browser features.** `Permissions-Policy` disables every
+   powerful API by default. Geolocation and Payment are granted to their own
+   page only, first-party only.
+
+## Third-party audit (2026-11-19)
+
+| Vendor / origin | Was used for | Data exposed | Decision |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `images.unsplash.com` | Hero background image | Visitor IP, User-Agent, Referer (page URL) on every page view | **Removed.** Image (Unsplash License) now self-hosted at `assets/img/hero-coffee.jpg`. Checked: no EXIF/GPS metadata. |
+| Analytics / tag managers | — | — | None present. Not to be added without a review (see below). |
+| Web fonts (Google Fonts, Typekit) | — | — | None. The site uses system fonts. |
+| Social embeds / pixels | — | — | None. |
+
+**Current third-party requests: 0.**
+
+### Adding a vendor
+A new third party needs: a documented purpose, a list of data fields shared, a
+signed DPA, a retention period, and consent gating if the vendor is non-essential.
+After approval, add its origin to `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` in `scripts/privacy-audit.mjs`
+and to the CSP in *both* `index.html` and `_headers`, then update the table above.
+
+## Data inventory (client side)
+
+| Data | Where | Purpose | Retention |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Session cookie (set by backend) | Cookie, should be `HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Lax`, `__Host-` prefix | Authentication | Session; cleared on logout via `Clear-Site-Data` |
+| `dg:*` keys | local/sessionStorage (none set today) | Reserved for app UI state. **Never store PII or tokens here.** | Cleared on logout |
+| Privacy signal | Read from `navigator.globalPrivacyControl` | Opt-out of sale/share | Not stored |
+
+## Files
+
+- `index.html`: no inline code, meta CSP, referrer policy, POST logout, privacy-choices link and GPC notice.
+- `assets/js/privacy.js`: GPC/DNT handling, URL PII stripping, outbound `noopener noreferrer`, logout storage wipe, bfcache guard for pages marked `data-requires-auth`. Makes no network calls.
+- `_headers`: CSP (adds `frame-ancestors`), HSTS, COOP/CORP/COEP, Permissions-Policy, per-route Cache-Control, Clear-Site-Data.
+- `.well-known/gpc.json`: GPC support declaration.
+- `scripts/privacy-audit.mjs`: automated guardrail.
+
+## Backend requirements (outside this repo)
+
+- `POST /logout` must check a CSRF token or `Origin`/`Sec-Fetch-Site`, invalidate the session server-side, and respond with the `Clear-Site-Data` header (declared in `_headers`).
+- Serve the `_headers` set from whatever host is in use. The local `statikk` dev server ignores them. Only the meta CSP and referrer policy apply locally.
+- Treat a GPC signal (`Sec-GPC: 1`) as an opt-out of sale/sharing on the server too.
+- Implement `/privacy-choices` and `/privacy-policy`.
